    slug: "when-nosql",
    shortDescription: "Provide decision criteria.",
    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nChoose NoSQL for: massive scale, high write throughput, flexible schema, or when data is unstructured. Choose SQL for: strong consistency, complex queries (joins), and ACID transactions.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThe interviewer wants the reasoning behind when would you choose a nosql database over a sql database, not just the definition. Explain the problem it solves and the condition that would make you choose another approach.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Choose NoSQL for: massive scale, high write throughput, flexible schema, or when data is unstructured.\n2. Choose SQL for: strong consistency, complex queries (joins), and ACID transactions.\n3. Connect the concept to latency, failure modes, capacity, consistency, and operational cost rather than discussing components in isolation..\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nFocus on judgment: what need makes this useful, and what assumption would change your recommendation?\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a production application, an engineer can use the concept in a concrete query or transaction and verify the resulting rows, locks, or execution plan. Choose NoSQL for: massive scale, high write throughput, flexible schema, or when data is unstructured.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn a production platform, when would you choose a nosql database over a sql database affects component boundaries, capacity, latency, consistency, or failure handling. The design should start from traffic and reliability assumptions, then choose the simplest architecture that meets them.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Giving a definition instead of answering the reason or decision.\n- Stating an absolute rule without assumptions.\n- Missing the condition that would make another approach preferable.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nTie the reason to a concrete requirement or failure mode. A “why” answer is stronger when it explains what would make the recommendation change.",
